governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (All 7 failures were in the acceptance tests' own setup, not the implementations: the store must be created inside an injection context (NG0203, its constructor registers a signal effect) and the watchlist page's routerLink needs router providers (NG0201). Rewriting both acceptance tests accordingly; the round-1 clearWatched contracts are unchanged and re-issued as verification instructions.)
round 2: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 3: accept  (The oracle is fully green (tsc exit 0, 46 vitest tests passing). WatchlistStore exposes clearWatched(): void which removes every watched (seen) item, keeps items/count/watchedCount consistent, persists the result, and is a safe no-op when nothing is watched; the Watchlist page renders a "Clear seen movies" button (only while at least one movie is seen) that calls it and announces how many were removed. The acceptance tests for both units exercise this end-to-end behaviour and all pass, so the request is satisfied.)

